<td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(20190)">UWO ID 20190 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">1. Prod Stopped</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Toilet Partitions</td><td class="" role="gridcell"></td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">There seems to be a leak coming from what looks like one of the pipes above located in the TPF packing area. When time permits could we have you guys take a look at this please.
</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Maintenance</td><td class="" role="gridcell">8/3/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"></td></tr><tr class="k-alt k-master-row" data-uid="d904c867-2cce-4247-a43c-cc5f92027cb2" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(17233)">UWO ID 17233 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">2. General Maint - High Priority</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Soap Dispenser Assembly</td><td class="" role="gridcell">B-822 Tester - Cell 1 (3 nests)</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">Cell 1 Tester Light isn't working for the Middle Nest. No Red/Green light, can't tell if the unit passed or failed.</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Maintenance</td><td class="" role="gridcell">10/9/2025</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"><span class="pmpt-bob">Primo Uy - 10/21/25  3:08:53 PM:&nbsp;</span>Red (Fail) light is working but Green is still not working, it stays on (lights), it looks like its stack. I need ME to take a look at it; it could be the PLC program need to be updated or check.
</td></tr><tr class="k-master-row" data-uid="cf402e55-b798-4b69-a0f3-136e2eab2ccf" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(19004)">UWO ID 19004 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">2. General Maint - High Priority</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Toilet Partitions</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Drill Jig - OS Door Hinge </td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">After a recent CCR, we had a discussion with the team and some concerns were brought up that I was not previously aware of. One of the main issues is that the jig can shift during use, which is leading to rework and, in this case, CCRs.

Could we get your help to review and fix the current jig, and possibly look into creating an improved version?</td><td class="" role="gridcell">M/E</td><td class="" role="gridcell">4/7/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"><span class="pmpt-bob">Gabriel Shinobi - 05/01/26  7:44:43 AM:&nbsp;</span>Per M/E Eric, QA request has been submitted to inspect the jig, as well is currently investigating the issue
</td></tr><tr class="k-alt k-master-row" data-uid="81d07b3f-0f35-4641-8427-7e5d608f8aa1" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(19941)">UWO ID 19941 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">2. General Maint - High Priority</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Toilet Partitions</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Drill Jig - OS Door Hinge </td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">Jig is slightly off on the latch, might be time for a new jig.</td><td class="" role="gridcell">M/E</td><td class="" role="gridcell">6/24/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"></td></tr><tr class="k-master-row" data-uid="538b320a-21c3-440c-b5b9-0fe40e11da35" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(20281)">UWO ID 20281 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">2. General Maint - High Priority</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Shipping</td><td class="" role="gridcell">#22 Jungheinrich  VNA Forklift</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">High reach arm not working and machine stuck in aisle A/B. Not moving due to broken arm.</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Maintenance</td><td class="" role="gridcell">8/6/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"><span class="pmpt-bob">Gabriel Shinobi - 08/13/26  7:58:24 AM:&nbsp;</span>Tech, ordered part, waiting on tech to return
</td></tr><tr class="k-alt k-master-row" data-uid="2be54155-0cc6-40d5-b350-8733bf77ebb4" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(20424)">UWO ID 20424 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">2. General Maint - High Priority</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Soap Dispenser Assembly</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Cartoner, 822, Econoseal E-System 2000 #1</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">Cartoner is not getting air and checked sensors they are engaged.  </td><td class="" role="gridcell">Maintenance</td><td class="" role="gridcell">8/19/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"><span class="pmpt-bob">Primo Uy - 08/25/26  1:10:12 PM:&nbsp;</span>8/25/25 at 1.10 PM
Cartoner still working properly and i will contenue the monitoring until the rest of the day.
</td></tr><tr class="k-master-row" data-uid="420e659c-cffb-4a4e-9be8-5b46ae758904" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(18452)">UWO ID 18452 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Toilet Partitions</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Insert 1 Screwdriver, Auto Reverse, Lever</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">we are using the last good insert screwdriver on the CL line the rest of the are eider in maintenance getting fix or no good at all shinobi I know you were looking in to getting a new one.  please see if we can get it if the one, we are using breaks we won't have any replacement</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Maintenance</td><td class="" role="gridcell">2/11/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"><span class="pmpt-bob">Gabriel Shinobi - 05/01/26  8:14:00 AM:&nbsp;</span>sent back, drivers had the incorrect heads on them waiting for drivers to be received
</td></tr><tr class="k-alt k-master-row" data-uid="e35d8af7-5015-4b75-907c-1704f9c161fb" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(18742)">UWO ID 18742 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Toilet Partitions</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Drilling Machine CNC, 1040 Laminate </td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">Hi, Gannomat somehow glitched and drilled a program incorrectly for a 4.5" FC stile instead of 9"FC through the standard program packet. We retested the same program with a sample PB piece where it correctly drilled for 4.5"FC this time. Can we take a look at this as this will cause issue more down the production hours? thank you</td><td class="" role="gridcell">M/E</td><td class="" role="gridcell">3/12/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"></td></tr><tr class="k-master-row" data-uid="d7846b7b-51f4-4a69-b70f-85672951821a" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(19989)">UWO ID 19989 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Toilet Partitions</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Saw, 10' Panel, Laminate Line</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell">Laminate guide is off. Leaving laminate cut as uneven. </td><td class="" role="gridcell">Maintenance</td><td class="" role="gridcell">6/30/2026</td><td class="k-textarea-cell" role="gridcell"></td></tr><tr class="k-alt k-master-row" data-uid="1edacc8c-e621-40df-a3ac-f985d92a02e1" role="row"><td class="" role="gridcell"><a class="id-links" title="Edit Work Order" href="#" onclick="WorkOrderHomeMgr.EditWorkOrderUnschd(20497)">UWO ID 20497 </a></td><td class="" role="gridcell">3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped</td><td class="" role="gridcell">Toilet Partitions</td><td class="" role